---
import ArrowIcon from "../components/ArrowIcon.astro";
import CtaBand from "../components/CtaBand.astro";
import CopyTextButton from "../components/CopyTextButton.astro";
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { site } from "../data/site";

const installCommand = `composer create-project ph7software/ph7builder:${site.latestRelease} my-dating-app --no-dev --prefer-dist`;
---

<BaseLayout title="pH7Builder for AI builders" description="Give Codex, Claude Code or another AI coding agent an established open-source dating and community foundation to understand, customise and test." path="/ai-builders/">
  <header class="page-hero shell">
    <p class="eyebrow">pH7Builder for AI builders</p>
    <h1>Give your agent a foundation worth extending.</h1>
    <p class="lede">pH7Builder is a versioned PHP application with working product domains, documented project decisions and automated checks. Your agent can focus on the parts that make the customer’s product different.</p>
    <div class="hero-actions">
      <a class="button" href="/build/">Generate a product blueprint<ArrowIcon /></a>
      <a class="text-link" href={site.githubUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Explore the repository<ArrowIcon /><span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="section surface">
    <div class="shell install-grid">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">A real starting point</p>
        <h2>Install the application, not another blank repository.</h2>
        <p class="lede">Composer gives an agent a repeatable way to obtain the published source. The generated application is an independent project copy, so future upstream upgrades remain an explicit, testable operation.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="terminal" aria-label="Composer installation command">
        <div class="terminal-bar"><span></span><span></span><span></span><b>terminal</b></div>
        <pre><code><span>$</span> composer create-project \
  ph7software/ph7builder:{site.latestRelease} \
  my-dating-app --no-dev --prefer-dist</code></pre>
        <CopyTextButton value={installCommand} label="Copy command" successMessage="Command copied." tone="dark" />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <div><p class="eyebrow">What the agent receives</p><h2>Context before code generation.</h2></div>
        <p>The project guide explains architecture, security invariants, conventions and verification. The product blueprint adds the customer’s intent without pretending every proposed key already exists in the software.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="agent-context-grid">
        {[
          ["01", "Application foundation", "Existing identity, discovery, messaging, membership, moderation and administration domains."],
          ["02", "Repository contract", "An AGENTS.md guide that tells coding agents where changes belong and which security boundaries must remain intact."],
          ["03", "Portable intent", "A blueprint that records the audience, business rules, desired experience, privacy decisions and launch requirements."],
          ["04", "Verification", "Unit, static-analysis and repository checks that give an agent concrete evidence instead of confidence by assertion."],
        ].map(([number, title, description]) => (
          <article><span>{number}</span><h3>{title}</h3><p>{description}</p></article>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section surface">
    <div class="shell readiness-grid">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">The honest state</p>
        <h2>AI-ready is a direction with evidence, not a sticker.</h2>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3>Available now</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Composer project distribution</li>
          <li>Repository-wide agent instructions</li>
          <li>Official skills for installation, module development and upgrade preflight</li>
          <li>A browser-only blueprint generator</li>
          <li>Documented installation and production requirements</li>
          <li>Automated tests and static analysis</li>
        </ul>
        <h3>Deliberate next steps</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Stable extension points for more customer changes outside core</li>
          <li>A documented API surface for web, mobile and agent clients</li>
          <li>A product passport that records upstream version and custom areas</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section shell">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">A safer agent workflow</p><h2>Make every change explainable and reversible.</h2></div>
      <p>Fast generation is useful. Long-term maintainability comes from explicit scope, small commits, behavioural tests and a record of why the product differs from upstream.</p>
    </div>
    <ol class="workflow-list">
      <li><b>Describe</b><span>Capture the customer, business model, safety requirements and desired member journey.</span></li>
      <li><b>Map</b><span>Identify which needs already exist in pH7Builder and which require extension.</span></li>
      <li><b>Implement</b><span>Keep custom behaviour at the narrowest appropriate layer and avoid core edits where an extension point works.</span></li>
      <li><b>Prove</b><span>Run focused behavioural checks, then the wider deterministic suite before publication.</span></li>
      <li><b>Record</b><span>Update the product blueprint and preserve small Git commits so the next agent can continue safely.</span></li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <CtaBand eyebrow="Give your agent a useful brief" title="Start with a product decision, not a pile of files." primaryLabel="Create the blueprint" primaryHref="/build/" secondaryLabel="See Nomad Connections" secondaryHref="/blueprints/nomad-connections/" />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .install-grid,
  .readiness-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    align-items: center;
    gap: clamp(3rem, 8vw, 8rem);
  }

  .terminal {
    padding-bottom: 1.5rem;
    border: 2px solid var(--ink);
    border-radius: 0.75rem;
    background: var(--ink);
    color: white;
    box-shadow: 8px 8px 0 var(--coral);
  }

  .terminal-bar {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.4rem;
    padding: 0.75rem 1rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid #454b60;
  }

  .terminal-bar span {
    width: 0.7rem;
    height: 0.7rem;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--coral);
  }

  .terminal-bar span:nth-child(2) { background: var(--yellow); }
  .terminal-bar span:nth-child(3) { background: var(--lime); }
  .terminal-bar b { margin-left: auto; color: #9da4ba; font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 0.7rem; }
  .terminal pre { padding: 2rem 1.5rem 1rem; margin: 0; overflow-x: auto; font-family: var(--mono); }
  .terminal code span { color: var(--lime); }
  .agent-context-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    border: 2px solid var(--ink);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .agent-context-grid article { min-height: 16rem; padding: 1.75rem; border: 1px solid var(--ink); background: var(--paper-strong); }
  .agent-context-grid span { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 0.7rem; font-weight: 800; }
  .agent-context-grid h3 { margin-top: 3rem; }
  .agent-context-grid p { color: var(--ink-soft); }

  .readiness-grid { align-items: start; }
  .readiness-grid h3 { margin-top: 0; padding-top: 0.5rem; border-top: 2px solid var(--ink); }
  .readiness-grid h3:not(:first-child) { margin-top: 2.5rem; }
  .readiness-grid li + li { margin-top: 0.55rem; }

  .workflow-list { padding: 0; margin: 0; list-style: none; counter-reset: workflow; border-top: 2px solid var(--ink); }
  .workflow-list li { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(8rem, 0.35fr) 1fr; gap: 2rem; padding: 1.4rem 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .workflow-list b { font-family: var(--serif); font-size: 1.5rem; }
  .workflow-list span { color: var(--ink-soft); }

  @media (max-width: 760px) {
    .install-grid,
    .readiness-grid,
    .agent-context-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .workflow-list li { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 0.25rem; }
  }
</style>
